      "Language": "bul",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The aim of the authors was to investigate reliability of method, used by them, for diagnosis of extrauterine pregnancy EP (EP). 123 women with admission diagnosis: obs. graviditas extrauterine were studied retrospectively. It was established that the abdominal pain together with the triad of symptoms from the vaginal-abdominal examination: congested adnexae, enlarged uterus and painful cavum Douglasi were of great diagnostic significance. The highly predicting value and sensitivity of ultrasound examination women with EP emphasized the substantial contribution of echography for early and exact diagnosis, which together with timely operative intervention could contribute to preserve the reproductive capability of women."},
